  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nThe latest REFS model from this morning has a shortwave trough\naround 2 PM today and then another one around 9 PM riding through\nthe upper ridge. This along with southeasterly flow near the\nsurface and water vapor moving in will give a chance for showers\nand thunderstorms tonight, and then again tomorrow evening. There\nis potential for severe winds in the west tonight. A trough is\nexpected to bring temperatures down about 10 degrees this weekend,\nand showers and storms are expected. There is a decent chance of a\nfew locations receiving at least a wetting rain on Sunday, and a\nslight chance of exceeding a quarter inch. The ECMWF and GFS\nensembles both indicate that northeast Montana will be situated\nbetween an upper ridge and trough next week, but certainty is low\non the exact pattern.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nOnly deviation to NBM was to PoPs through Saturday evening.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence of showers and storms\naffecting various parts of the area trough Sunday evening. There\nis moderate to high confidence of a wetting rain occurring this\nweekend, and low confidence on areas receiving over a quarter of\nan inch.\n\nThere is low to moderate confidence in severe winds occurring late\nthis evening.\n\nThere is low to moderate confidence on whether an upper ridge will\nbuild in again early next week.",
